{"availability":"available","full":"RPBMedia/story-maker","name":"story-maker","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-19T13:40:44Z","updated":"2026-10-08T07:03:23Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://story-maker-mu.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://story-maker-mu.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:37.687Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:37.687Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:37.687Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:35:37.687Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Turn a soundtrack, photos and video clips into a finished video, entirely in the browser. Nothing is uploaded: the video is made on the device, with WebCodecs (fast, Chrome and Safari 16.4+) and ffmpeg.wasm as the fallback. Live at","In-browser encoding is CPU- and memory-bound: wasm FFmpeg is single-threaded here and the whole filesystem lives in RAM (with a 2 GB address-space ceiling). 1280×720@30 renders reliably at roughly real-time speed on ordinary hardware; 1080p roughly doubles pixel throughput and memory pressure, turning \"works everywhere\" into \"works on fast machines with patience.\"","RenderSettings already models width/height/fps, so adding a 1920×1080 option later is a settings-UI change plus a memory warning — no pipeline changes. Cloud rendering (see roadmap) is the honest path to fast high-res exports."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RPBMedia/story-maker/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3ce502d6cec81cfa3ff46122d6ad621843c938d310bfe289e1499d7520532b76","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:37.840Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:37.840Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Turn a soundtrack, photos and video clips into a finished video, entirely in the browser. Nothing is uploaded: the video is made on the device, with WebCodecs (fast, Chro